5799797575b', 'content': \"1\\timport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest'\\n2\\timport { loginAction, registerAction, logoutAction } from '../actions/auth'\\n3\\timport type { LoginInput, RegisterInput } from '../schemas/auth'\\n4\\t\\n5\\t// Mock the supabase client module\\n6\\tvi.mock('../lib/supabase/server', () => {\\n7\\t  const mockSupabaseClient = {\\n8\\t    auth: {\\n9\\t      signInWithPassword: vi.fn(),\\n10\\t      signUp: vi.fn(),\\n11\\t      signOut: vi.fn(),\\n12\\t    },\\n13\\t  }\\n14\\t  return {\\n15\\t    createClient: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockSupabaseClient),\\n16\\t  }\\n17\\t})\\n18\\t\\n19\\t// Mock Next.js navigation\\n20\\tvi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\\n21\\t  redirect: vi.fn(),\\n22\\t  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\\n23\\t}))\\n24\\t\\n25\\t// Mock Next.js cache\\n26\\tvi.mock('next/cache', () => ({\\n27\\t  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\\n28\\t}))\\n29\\t\\n30\\timport { createClient } from '../lib/supabase/server'\\n31\\timport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\\n32\\timport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\\n33\\t\\n34\\tdescribe('loginAction', () => {\\n35\\t  beforeEach(() => {\\n36\\t    vi.clearAllMocks()\\n37\\t  })\\n38\\t\\n39\\t  it('should successfully login an admin user and redirect to admin dashboard', async () => {\\n40\\t    const input: LoginInput = {\\n41\\t      email: 'admin@example.com',\\n42\\t      password: 'password123',\\n43\\t    }\\n44\\t\\n45\\t    const mockUser = {\\n46\\t      id: 'user-123',\\n47\\t      email: 'admin@example.com',\\n48\\t      user_metadata: { role: 'admin' },\\n49\\t    }\\n50\\t\"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': \" see the problem: line 22 and 31 are trying to import `revalidatePath` from `next/navigation`, which doesn't exist. That's a mistake. I should remove that from the mock and from the import. Only `next/cache` has `revalidatePath`. I'll fix it.\\n\\nAlso line 32: import { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache' - that is correct.\\n\\nSo I need to modify:\\n- In the mock for next/navigation, remove the revalidatePath entry (keep only redirect)\\n- In the import statement on line 31, only import redirect\\n\\nLet me edit that file.\\n\\nI need to fix the import - `next/navigation` doesn't export `revalidatePath`. I'll correct the mock and imports:\", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_d654d3d145a54ec7a7e075a5', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Edit', 'arguments': '{\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"c:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\ADMIN\\\\\\\\Desktop\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\projects\\\\\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\__tests__\\\\\\\\auth.actions.test.ts\", \"old_string\": \"// Mock Next.js navigation\\\\nvi.mock(\\'next/navigation\\', () => ({\\\\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\\\\n  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\\\\n}))\", \"new_string\": \"// Mock Next.js navigation\\\\nvi.mock(\\'next/navigation\\', () => ({\\\\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\\\\n}))\"}'}}, {'id': 'call_8bdbc08b05394e9f84dfb3e5', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Edit', 'arguments': '{\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"c:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\ADMIN\\\\\\\\Desktop\\\\\\\\workspace\\\\\\\\projects\\\\\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\__tests__\\\\\\\\auth.actions.test.ts\", \"old_string\": \"import { createClient } from \\'../lib/supabase/server\\'\\\\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from \\'next/navigation\\'\\\\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from \\'next/cache\\'\", \"new_string\": \"import { createClient } from \\'../lib/supabase/server\\'\\\\nimport { redirect } from \\'next/navigation\\'\\\\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from \\'next/cache\\'\"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_d654d3d145a54ec7a7e075a5', 'content': 'The file c:\\\\Users\\\\ADMIN\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\src\\\\__tests__\\\\auth.actions.test.ts has been updated successfully. (file state is current