Only `next/cache` has `revalidatePath`. I'll fix it.\n\nAlso line 32: import { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache' - that is correct.\n\nSo I need to modify:\n- In the mock for next/navigation, remove the revalidatePath entry (keep only redirect)\n- In the import statement on line 31, only import redirect\n\nLet me edit that file.\n\nI need to fix the import - `next/navigation` doesn't export `revalidatePath`. I'll correct the mock and imports:"}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "call_d654d3d145a54ec7a7e075a5", "name": "Edit", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\src\\__tests__\\auth.actions.test.ts", "old_string": "// Mock Next.js navigation\nvi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\n  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\n}))", "new_string": "// Mock Next.js navigation\nvi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\n}))"}}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "call_8bdbc08b05394e9f84dfb3e5", "name": "Edit", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\src\\__tests__\\auth.actions.test.ts", "old_string": "import { createClient } from '../lib/supabase/server'\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'", "new_string": "import { createClient } from '../lib/supabase/server'\nimport { redirect } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'"}}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "call_d654d3d145a54ec7a7e075a5", "content": "The file c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\src\\__tests__\\auth.actions.test.ts has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)"}, {"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "call_8bdbc