re tsconfig to support vitest.\n\nBut first, add test scripts to package.json.\n\n now add test scripts to package.json:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_809f23d871cb494cb9abb5e5", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"c:\\\\Users\\\\ADMIN\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\package.json\", \"old_string\": \"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"next dev\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"next build\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"next start\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"next lint\\\"\\n  },\", \"new_string\": \"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"next dev\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"next build\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"next start\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"next lint\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"vitest\\\",\\n    \\\"test:ui\\\": \\\"vitest --ui\\\",\\n    \\\"test:coverage\\\": \\\"vitest run --coverage\\\"\\n  },\"}"}}, {"id": "call_cbf7ea96f4fb4a11a600802d", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Installing Vitest and testing dependencies\", \"content\": \"Install Vitest and testing dependencies\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Configuring Vitest setup\", \"content\": \"Configure Vitest (vitest.config.ts)\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Writing schema validation tests\", \"content\": \"Write unit tests for Zod schemas (auth.ts)\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Writing server action tests\", \"content\": \"Write unit tests for login/register server actions\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Adding test scripts to package.json\", \"content\": \"Add test scripts to package.json\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Running tests to verify\", \"content\": \"Run tests and verify all pass\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_809f23d871cb494cb9abb5e5", "content": "The file c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\package.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_cbf7ea96f4fb4a11a600802d", "content": "Todos have been modified successfully. Ensure that you continue to use the todo list to track your progress. Please proceed with the current tasks if applicable"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": " I need to write the actual tests. I'll write comprehensive tests for:\n1. Zod schemas - testing all validation rules for login, register, forgot email, reset password\n2. Server actions - I'll need to mock Supabase client and Next.js navigation functions\n\nLet me start with the schema tests first as those are isolated and easier.\n\nNow let's write the unit tests! I'll start with the Zod schema tests (pure validation) and then the server action tests (with mocking).Now let's write comprehensive tests for the schemas and auth actions:\n\n## 1. Schema Tests (pure Zod validation)\n\nwill create a test file for the auth schemas:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_3e6a22c8311346d5822255e3", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"c:\\\\Users\\\\ADMIN\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\src\\\\__tests__\\\\auth.schema.test.ts\", \"content\": \"import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'\\nimport {\\n  loginSchema,\\n  registerSchema,\\n  forgotPasswordSchema,\\n  resetPasswordSchema,\\n  type LoginInput,\\n  type RegisterInput,\\n} from '../schemas/auth'\\n\\ndescribe('loginSchema', () => {\\n  it('should validate correct login data', () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'test@example.com',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n    const result = loginSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing email', () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: '',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n    const result = loginSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toBe('Email is required')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject invalid email format', () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'invalid-email',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n    const result = loginSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toBe('Enter a valid email address')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing password', () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'test@example.com',\\n      password: '',\\n    }\\n    const result = loginSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toBe('Password is required')\\n    }\\n  })\\n})\\n\\ndescribe('registerSchema', () => {\\n  const validRegisterInput: RegisterInput = {\\n    firstName: 'John',\\n    surname: 'Doe',\\n    email: 'john@example.com',\\n    sex: 'male',\\n    birthday: '1990-01-15',\\n    nationality: 'American',\\n    address: '123 Main St',\\n    phoneNumber: '+1234567890',\\n    password: 'SecurePass123',\\n    confirmPassword: 'SecurePass123',\\n  }\\n\\n  it('should validate correct registration data', () => {\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(validRegisterInput)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing firstName', () => {\\n    const { firstName, ...rest } = validRegisterInput\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(rest)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toContain('First Name is required')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject firstName with less than 2 characters', () => {\\n    const input = { ...validRegisterInput, firstName: 'J' }\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toContain('at least 2 characters')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing surname', () => {\\n    const { surname, ...rest } = validRegisterInput\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(rest)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toContain('surname is required')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject invalid email', () => {\\n    const input = { ...validRegisterInput, email: 'not-an-email' }\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject invalid sex enum value', () => {\\n    const input = { ...validRegisterInput, sex: 'other' as const }\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should accept optional sex field', () => {\\n    const { sex, ...rest } = validRegisterInput\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(rest)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject short password', () => {\\n    const input = { ...validRegisterInput, password: '12345' }\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toContain('at least 8 characters')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject mismatched passwords', () => {\\n    const input = {\\n      ...validRegisterInput,\\n      confirmPassword: 'DifferentPassword123',\\n    }\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toBe('Passwords do not match')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should accept missing optional age field', () => {\\n    const { age, ...rest } = validRegisterInput\\n    const result = registerSchema.safeParse(rest)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n})\\n\\ndescribe('forgotPasswordSchema', () => {\\n  it('should validate correct email', () => {\\n    const input = { email: 'test@example.com' }\\n    const result = forgotPasswordSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing email', () => {\\n    const input = { email: '' }\\n    const result = forgotPasswordSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject invalid email format', () => {\\n    const input = { email: 'invalid' }\\n    const result = forgotPasswordSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n})\\n\\ndescribe('resetPasswordSchema', () => {\\n  const validInput = {\\n    password: 'NewStrongPassword123',\\n    confirmPassword: 'NewStrongPassword123',\\n  }\\n\\n  it('should validate matching passwords', () => {\\n    const result = resetPasswordSchema.safeParse(validInput)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject short password', () => {\\n    const input = { password: '12345', confirmPassword: '12345' }\\n    const result = resetPasswordSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject mismatched passwords', () => {\\n    const input = {\\n      password: 'Password123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'DifferentPassword123',\\n    }\\n    const result = resetPasswordSchema.safeParse(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    if (!result.success) {\\n      expect(result.error.issues[0].message).toBe('Passwords do not match')\\n    }\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should reject missing confirmPassword', () => {\\n    const { confirmPassword, ...rest } = validInput\\n    const result = resetPasswordSchema.safeParse(rest)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n  })\\n})\\n\"}"}}, {"id": "call_28fc3eae77c94e5f94acfbb0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Installing Vitest and testing dependencies\", \"content\": \"Install Vitest and testing dependencies\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Configuring Vitest setup\", \"content\": \"Configure Vitest (vitest.config.ts)\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Writing schema validation tests\", \"content\": \"Write unit tests for Zod schemas (auth.ts)\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Writing server action tests\", \"content\": \"Write unit tests for login/register server actions\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Adding test scripts to package.json\", \"content\": \"Add test scripts to package.json\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Running tests to verify\", \"content\": \"Run tests and verify all pass\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_3e6a22c8311346d5822255e3", "content": "File created successfully at: c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\src\\__tests__\\auth.schema.test.ts (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_28fc3eae77c94e5f94acfbb0", "content": "Todos have been modified successfully. Ensure that you continue to use the todo list to track your progress. Please proceed with the current tasks if applicable"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "! Now I need to write tests for the server actions. The server actions depend on:\n- Supabase client (need to mock)\n- Next.js navigation (redirect, revalidatePath) - need to mock\n\nLooking at the auth.ts file, the functions:\n- loginAction: uses supabase.auth.signInWithPassword, redirect, revalidatePath\n- registerAction: uses supabase.auth.signUp, redirect, revalidatePath\n- forgotPasswordAction: uses supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail\n- resetPasswordAction: uses supabase.auth.updateUser, revalidatePath, redirect\n- logoutAction: uses supabase.auth.signOut, revalidatePath, redirect\n- getSession: uses supabase.auth.getUser\n- oauthAction: uses supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth, redirect\n\nFor testing server actions, I need to mock:\n1. The supabase client (the createClient function)\n2. Next.js navigation functions (redirect, revalidatePath) - these throw in Next.js so we can mock them to do nothing or capture calls\n\nHowever, there's a challenge: The auth.ts file uses 'use server' directive and server actions. Testing server actions can be tricky because they're designed to run on the server. But for unit testing, we can:\n- Test the internal logic by calling the functions directly (they're async functions)\n- Mock the supabase client that createClient returns\n\nLet me create a mock for supabase and test the login and register actions.\n\nI'll create a helper mock file first.\n\nLet me also think about how to mock createClient. The createClient function is imported from '@/lib/supabase/server'. I need to either:\n1. Mock the entire module using vi.mock()\n2. Create a wrapper that makes it easier to test\n\nOption 1 is more straightforward for unit tests. I'll use Vitest's mocking capabilities.\n\nI'll need to also mock the redirect and revalidatePath functions from next/navigation and next/cache. In Next.js, these functions throw special errors to terminate the server action and redirect. For unit testing, I can mock them to either:\n- Track calls without throwing\n- Or throw a special mock error that we catch to assert behavior\n\nActually simpler: I can re-export them from next/navigation and provide test doubles that just capture the arguments without throwing.\n\n\nI'll create a comprehensive test suite that covers various scenarios:\n\n1. Test login success with valid credentials\n2. Test login failure with wrong password\n3. Test register success\n4. Test register with validation failure\n5. Test forgot password with valid email\n6. Test reset password success\n7. Test logout\n8. Test oauth\n\nI'll focus on login and register as requested. Let me write a test file for auth.actions.\n\nGreat! Schema tests done. Now let's write tests for the server actions (login/register). I'll need to mock Supabase and Next.js navigation functions.\n\nLet me create the server actions test with proper mocking:will create auth.actions.test.ts:\n\nLet's write the server action tests with proper mocking. I'll use vi.mock to mock the supabase module and Next.js functions:Now I'll create comprehensive tests for the auth server actions, mocking Supabase and Next.js dependencies:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_db9e6d7538ad4af1a72dffce", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"c:\\\\Users\\\\ADMIN\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\projects\\\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\\\src\\\\__tests__\\\\auth.actions.test.ts\", \"content\": \"import { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest'\\nimport { loginAction, registerAction, logoutAction } from '../actions/auth'\\nimport type { LoginInput, RegisterInput } from '../schemas/auth'\\n\\n// Mock the supabase client module\\nvi.mock('../lib/supabase/server', () => {\\n  const mockSupabaseClient = {\\n    auth: {\\n      signInWithPassword: vi.fn(),\\n      signUp: vi.fn(),\\n      signOut: vi.fn(),\\n    },\\n  }\\n  return {\\n    createClient: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockSupabaseClient),\\n  }\\n})\\n\\n// Mock Next.js navigation\\nvi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\\n  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\\n}))\\n\\n// Mock Next.js cache\\nvi.mock('next/cache', () => ({\\n  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\\n}))\\n\\nimport { createClient } from '../lib/supabase/server'\\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\\n\\ndescribe('loginAction', () => {\\n  beforeEach(() => {\\n    vi.clearAllMocks()\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should successfully login an admin user and redirect to admin dashboard', async () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'admin@example.com',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const mockUser = {\\n      id: 'user-123',\\n      email: 'admin@example.com',\\n      user_metadata: { role: 'admin' },\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signInWithPassword: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: mockUser },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    // Mock redirect to throw to exit the function\\n    ;(redirect as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockImplementation(() => {\\n      throw new Error('Redirect')\\n    })\\n\\n    await expect(loginAction(input)).rejects.toThrow('Redirect')\\n\\n    expect(createClient).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)\\n    expect(redirect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/admin/dashboard')\\n    expect(cacheRevalidate).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/', 'layout')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should successfully login an applicant user and redirect to applicant dashboard', async () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'applicant@example.com',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const mockUser = {\\n      id: 'user-456',\\n      email: 'applicant@example.com',\\n      user_metadata: { role: 'applicant' },\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signInWithPassword: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: mockUser },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    ;(redirect as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockImplementation(() => {\\n      throw new Error('Redirect')\\n    })\\n\\n    await expect(loginAction(input)).rejects.toThrow('Redirect')\\n\\n    expect(redirect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/applicant/dashboard')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should redirect to home if user has no role', async () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'user@example.com',\\n      password: 'password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const mockUser = {\\n      id: 'user-789',\\n      email: 'user@example.com',\\n      user_metadata: {},\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signInWithPassword: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: mockUser },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    ;(redirect as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockImplementation(() => {\\n      throw new Error('Redirect')\\n    })\\n\\n    await expect(loginAction(input)).rejects.toThrow('Redirect')\\n    expect(redirect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should return error for invalid credentials', async () => {\\n    const input: LoginInput = {\\n      email: 'wrong@example.com',\\n      password: 'wrongpassword',\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signInWithPassword: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: null,\\n          error: { message: 'Invalid login credentials' },\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    const result = await loginAction(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    expect(result.error).toBe('Invalid login credentials')\\n  })\\n})\\n\\ndescribe('registerAction', () => {\\n  beforeEach(() => {\\n    vi.clearAllMocks()\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should successfully register a new user', async () => {\\n    const input: RegisterInput = {\\n      firstName: 'Jane',\\n      surname: 'Smith',\\n      email: 'jane@example.com',\\n      sex: 'female',\\n      birthday: '1995-05-20',\\n      nationality: 'Canadian',\\n      address: '456 Oak Ave',\\n      phoneNumber: '+15551234567',\\n      password: 'SecurePass123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'SecurePass123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const mockUser = {\\n      id: 'new-user-123',\\n      email: 'jane@example.com',\\n      user_metadata: {\\n        name: 'Jane Smith',\\n        sex: 'female',\\n        birthday: '1995-05-20',\\n        nationality: 'Canadian',\\n        address: '456 Oak Ave',\\n      },\\n      created_at: '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z',\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signUp: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: mockUser, session: null },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    // Mock revalidatePath and redirect\\n    ;(cacheRevalidate as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockImplementation(() => {})\\n    ;(redirect as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockImplementation(() => {\\n      throw new Error('Redirect')\\n    })\\n\\n    const result = await registerAction(input)\\n\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false) // Because no session (email confirmation required)\\n    expect(result.error).toContain('confirmation email')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should return error for invalid email', async () => {\\n    const input: RegisterInput = {\\n      firstName: 'John',\\n      surname: 'Doe',\\n      email: 'invalid-email',\\n      birthday: '1990-01-01',\\n      nationality: 'American',\\n      address: '123 Main St',\\n      phoneNumber: '1234567890',\\n      password: 'Password123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'Password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const result = await registerAction(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    expect(result.error).toContain('valid email address')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should capitalize first name and surname correctly', async () => {\\n    const input: RegisterInput = {\\n      firstName: 'jOHN',\\n      surname: 'dOE',\\n      email: 'test@example.com',\\n      birthday: '1990-01-01',\\n      nationality: 'American',\\n      address: '123 Main St',\\n      phoneNumber: '1234567890',\\n      password: 'Password123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'Password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    const mockUser = {\\n      id: 'user-123',\\n      email: 'test@example.com',\\n      user_metadata: {\\n        name: 'John Doe',\\n        birthday: '1990-01-01',\\n        nationality: 'American',\\n        address: '123 Main St',\\n      },\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signUp: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: mockUser as any, session: null },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    await registerAction(input)\\n\\n    expect(createClient).toHaveBeenCalled()\\n    // Verify that signUp was called with capitalized name\\n    const supabaseClient = (createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mock.results[0].value\\n    expect(supabaseClient.auth.signUp).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\\n      expect.objectContaining({\\n        options: expect.objectContaining({\\n          data: expect.objectContaining({\\n            name: 'John Doe',\\n          }),\\n        }),\\n      })\\n    )\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should handle signUp error gracefully', async () => {\\n    const input: RegisterInput = {\\n      firstName: 'John',\\n      surname: 'Doe',\\n      email: 'duplicate@example.com',\\n      birthday: '1990-01-01',\\n      nationality: 'American',\\n      address: '123 Main St',\\n      phoneNumber: '1234567890',\\n      password: 'Password123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'Password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signUp: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: null,\\n          error: { message: 'User already exists' },\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    const result = await registerAction(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    expect(result.error).toBe('User already exists')\\n  })\\n\\n  it('should return error if user creation fails', async () => {\\n    const input: RegisterInput = {\\n      firstName: 'John',\\n      surname: 'Doe',\\n      email: 'fail@example.com',\\n      birthday: '1990-01-01',\\n      nationality: 'American',\\n      address: '123 Main St',\\n      phoneNumber: '1234567890',\\n      password: 'Password123',\\n      confirmPassword: 'Password123',\\n    }\\n\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signUp: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\\n          data: { user: null, session: null },\\n          error: null,\\n        }),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    const result = await registerAction(input)\\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false)\\n    expect(result.error).toBe('Failed to create account. Please try again.')\\n  })\\n})\\n\\ndescribe('logoutAction', () => {\\n  it('should successfully logout', async () => {\\n    ;(createClient as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mockResolvedValue({\\n      auth: {\\n        signOut: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({}),\\n      },\\n    })\\n\\n    await logoutAction()\\n\\n    expect(createClient).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)\\n    expect(createClient().auth.signOut).toHaveBeenCalled()\\n    expect(cacheRevalidate).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/', 'layout')\\n    expect(redirect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/login')\\n  })\\n})\\n\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_db9e6d7538ad4af1a72dffce", "content": "File created successfully at: c:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\workspace\\projects\\Special-Resident-Retiree-s-Visa\\src\\__tests__\\auth.actions.test.ts (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Continue from where you left off."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "No response requested."}, {"role": "user", "content": "continue the test"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me fix the import in the test file and also add a couple of missing validation tests. I'll also add tests for the forgot password and reset password actions since they're part of auth.\n\nFirst, let me update the auth.actions.test.ts to correct imports and add more comprehensive validation tests:", "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to continue. Let me review where I left off: I just created the test files for schemas and server actions. I need to also consider that I might need to add test script to package.json (already done). Now I should run the tests to verify they pass.\n\nBut I see a potential issue: In my auth.actions.test.ts file, I'm mocking redirect from 'next/navigation' but also importing revalidatePath from 'next/cache'. However, in the actual auth.ts file, it imports revalidatePath from 'next/cache', not from 'next/navigation'. So I need to make sure the mock is set up correctly for both.\n\nLooking at auth.ts:\n```ts\nimport { redirect } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nSo both are imported separately. My mock for 'next/navigation' only mocks redirect. My mock for 'next/cache' only mocks revalidatePath. That's correct. However, in my test file I import revalidatePath from 'next/cache' again and then later I'm using cacheRevalidate. That should be fine.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: When the server action calls revalidatePath, it's calling the import from 'next/cache', not the one I'm mocking in the vitest module. My vitest.mock for 'next/cache' will replace the entire module, so when auth.ts imports revalidatePath, it will get the mock. But when my test file imports it, it also gets the mock. That's fine.\n\nI did a check: In the test file I do:\n```ts\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nWait, this is wrong. `next/navigation` doesn't export revalidatePath. That's a mistake. In auth.ts, revalidatePath comes from 'next/cache', not from 'next/navigation'. So in my test I should import redirect from 'next/navigation' and revalidatePath from 'next/cache'. I have that - but I also imported revalidatePath from 'next/navigation'? Let me read the code:\n\nFrom auth.actions.test.ts:\n```ts\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nAh! I incorrectly import revalidatePath from next/navigation. That's wrong because next/navigation doesn't have revalidatePath (at least not in recent Next.js). Actually in Next.js 14+, revalidatePath is from 'next/cache'. So I should remove that second import from next/navigation. Actually, I only need redirect from next/navigation. So I should fix that.\n\nLet me correct: I'll remove the revalidatePath from the first import line, and only import redirect from next/navigation. Then I'll import revalidatePath from next/cache and alias it for use in tests.\n\nActually my code says:\n```ts\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\n```\n\nThat's wrong. It should be:\n```ts\nimport { redirect } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nBut wait, I also want to mock revalidatePath from 'next/cache'. I already have a mock for 'next/cache' that re-exports revalidatePath as a mock function. So I can just import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache' in my test and use it. But then I'd have two different imports? Actually I can just import revalidatePath from 'next/cache' in the test file and use that directly. That would be cleaner.\n\nLet me adjust: In the test file, I'll just import:\n```ts\nimport { redirect } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nAnd then I'll have a separate mock for each module.\n\nBut in the mock for 'next/navigation' I provide mock for redirect; for 'next/cache' I provide mock for revalidatePath.\n\nLet's rewrite that test file more carefully.\n\nActually I think my current code is almost fine because I'm mocking both modules. However the import of revalidatePath from 'next/navigation' will fail at runtime (or it may be undefined). But the test file compiles because TypeScript might think it's there? No, it's wrong. I should fix it.\n\nLet me rewrite the import section properly.\n\nI'll update auth.actions.test.ts to correct imports.\n\nAlso I should think about making the mocks more robust. In the test file I'm using vi.mock which creates module-level mocks. That's fine.\n\nLet me also note: The registerAction tests use `redirect` and `revalidatePath` from Next.js. In the actual code, it uses `redirect` from 'next/navigation' and `revalidatePath` from 'next/cache'. So the mocks need to be for those exact modules.\n\nIn the test file I have:\n```ts\nvi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\n  redirect: vi.fn(),\n}))\nvi.mock('next/cache', () => ({\n  revalidatePath: vi.fn(),\n}))\n```\n\nBut I also import them in the test file:\n```ts\nimport { redirect, revalidatePath } from 'next/navigation'\nimport { revalidatePath as cacheRevalidate } from 'next/cache'\n```\n\nBut there's no revalidatePath in next/navigation, so the import will be undefined. But because I'm using vi.mock, these imports will get the mocked version anyway? Actually the vi.mock replaces the module exports, so if I try to import revalidatePath from 'next/navigation', it will try to read that property from the mocked module. Since my mock returns only { redirect: vi.fn() }, revalidatePath will be undefined. That would cause errors when I try to call it. But I'm not calling revalidatePath from the 'next/navigation' import; I'm calling cacheRevalidate which comes from the second import. So the undefined import is just an unused variable that might cause a lint error but not runtime. However I imported it, so it's there. But it's okay if it's undefined as long as I don't use it. But to avoid confusion, I should remove it.\n\nI'll fix that.\n\nNow also, I need to test that registerAction calls revalidatePath and redirect correctly. In my test for successful register (but with no session), I'm mocking revalidatePath to do nothing, and redirect to throw. I'm then checking that result.success is false (since no session). That test is okay.\n\nHowever, I need a test for successful register with session (immediate redirect). That would be when data.session exists. But the code currently logs \"confirmation email has been sent\" when !data.session. So that returns failure. That's for when email confirmation is required. But there might be a scenario where email confirmation is not required (maybe if email service is disabled?). Actually, according to the code, after signUp, if data.user && !data.session, it returns an error. So successful full login (immediate) only when data.session is present. That likely happens if email confirmation is disabled or if using auto-confirm in development.\n\nI could add a test for that scenario too. But for now, the current coverage is decent.\n\nLet's also test the registerAction's capitalize logic and that it calls signUp with the correct args. I already have a test for that.\n\nNow, also need to test forgotPasswordAction and resetPasswordAction? The user asked specifically for login and register, so I can do those. But for completeness, I can include them later if needed.\n\nNow, let me also consider that I need to test the schema validation, I've done that.\n\nBut there's one more thing: The server action tests need to properly mock the supabase client. In my code I'm mocking the entire module like:\n\n```ts\nvi.mock('../lib/supabase/server', () => {\n  const mockSupabaseClient = {\n    auth: {\n      signInWithPassword: vi.fn(),\n      signUp: vi.fn(),\n      signOut: vi.fn(),\n    },\n  }\n  return {\n    createClient: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockSupabaseClient),\n  }\n})\n```\n\nBut then later inside each test I'm re-mocking createClient with specific implementations. That's okay; vi.mock's implementation can be overridden per test with .mockResolvedValue again. However, I need to make sure that the mockSupabaseClient is actually used. Actually my vi.mock returns a factory that creates a new mockSupabaseClient each time? Since it's a function that returns the object, it's a fresh object on each module load? Actually vi.mock's factory is executed only once when the module is first imported. So it will create a single